---
/* Tranter's page change, « le rideau » (Sam, Nov 20: « quelque chose de plus unique à Tranter… clip mask… elevated »;
   his pick of three). Its job: carry the visitor from one page to the next in the menu's own gesture.
   - A link followed: the next page rises from the bottom as a curtain (a clip, --page-arrive-duration on
     --page-arrive-ease; Sam, 13:02: « balayage de bas en haut »), over the page being left, which drifts up a little
     (--page-shift) and dims (--page-dim). No coloured panel between the two. The bar is part of its page: its
     colours change as the curtain's edge reaches it, last.
   - From the open menu (Sam, 13:06: « la nouvelle page et son overlay par-dessus le menu »): the menu is part of the
     page being left; the curtain rises over it too, as it dims and drifts with its page. One gesture, nothing to sync.
   - The page that arrives (Sam, 14:53: « animer la page qui apparaît, les éléments… doux, bien dosé », no split
     text, no masks): it drifts up into place inside the curtain (--page-shift), and the blocks of its first two
     sections come in one after the other once the curtain has ended: a fade and a short rise
     (--page-enter-shift, --page-enter-duration on --page-enter-ease, --page-enter-stagger apart, --page-enter-wait
     after the curtain). An opening photo never fades (it is the page's largest paint): it settles from a slight zoom
     in its frame (--page-media-scale, --page-media-duration), as the menu's photo does. A page loaded directly opens
     the same way.
   - Reduced motion, or a browser without view transitions: a short crossfade, nothing travels.
   Every value is a token of base.css (system/gen.py). */
---

<style is:global>
  @layer components {
    html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition]::view-transition {
      background-color: var(--ink);
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      /* the arriving page's blocks, in reading order; the second section a beat after the first */
      html[data-page-transition="custom"] {
        --_enter-wait: var(--page-enter-wait);
        /* One thing at a time (Sam, Nov 21: « les éléments finissent pas leur animation, lag »): the blocks wait for the
           curtain to end, then come in on the page itself. Before, they came in under the curtain, the browser was
           busiest just as the page change ended, in the middle of their fade, and a wait that changed at that moment
           made them jump ahead. Paused, never re-timed: `data-astro-transition` is there for as long as the router's
           page change runs. */
        &[data-astro-transition] main > :nth-child(-n + 2) > .site-grid > * {
          animation-play-state: paused;
        }
        /* under the loading screen the opening waits for it to leave */
        &[data-loader="play"] main > :nth-child(-n + 2) > .site-grid :is(*, img) {
          animation-play-state: paused;
        }
        & main > :nth-child(-n + 2) > .site-grid > * {
          animation: tranter-page-enter var(--page-enter-duration) var(--page-enter-ease)
            calc(var(--_enter-wait) + (var(--_enter-section, 0) + var(--_enter-n, 0)) * var(--page-enter-stagger)) backwards;
          &:nth-child(2) { --_enter-n: 1; }
          &:nth-child(3) { --_enter-n: 2; }
          &:nth-child(4) { --_enter-n: 3; }
          &:nth-child(5) { --_enter-n: 4; }
          &:nth-child(n + 6) { --_enter-n: 5; }
        }
        & main > :nth-child(2) > .site-grid {
          --_enter-section: 3;
        }
        /* the opening's photo: opaque from the first paint, settling in its frame */
        & main > :first-child > .site-grid > :is(.media, :has(> .media)) {
          animation: none;
          & img {
            animation: tranter-page-settle var(--page-media-duration) var(--page-enter-ease) backwards;
          }
        }
      }
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition]::view-transition-old(root) {
        mix-blend-mode: normal;
        animation: tranter-page-leave var(--page-leave-duration) var(--page-leave-ease) both;
      }
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition]::view-transition-new(root) {
        mix-blend-mode: normal;
        animation: tranter-page-curtain var(--page-arrive-duration) var(--page-arrive-ease) both;
      }
      /* browsers without view transitions: Astro's fallback, a fade of the page's content */
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition-fallback="old"] body > :is(main, footer) {
        animation: tranter-page-fade var(--hover-duration) var(--hover-ease) both;
      }
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition-fallback="new"] body > :is(main, footer) {
        animation: tranter-page-fade var(--hover-duration) var(--hover-ease) reverse both;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition]::view-transition-group(*) {
        animation: none;
      }
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition]::view-transition-old(*) {
        animation: tranter-page-fade var(--hover-duration) linear both;
      }
      html[data-page-transition="custom"][data-astro-transition]::view-transition-new(*) {
        animation: tranter-page-fade var(--hover-duration) linear reverse both;
      }
    }

    @keyframes tranter-page-curtain {
      from {
        clip-path: inset(100% 0 0 0);
        translate: 0 var(--page-shift);
      }
      to {
        clip-path: inset(0 0 0 0);
      }
    }
    @keyframes tranter-page-leave {
      to {
        translate: 0 calc(var(--page-shift) * -1);
        opacity: var(--page-dim);
      }
    }
    @keyframes tranter-page-enter {
      from {
        opacity: 0;
        translate: 0 var(--page-enter-shift);
      }
    }
    @keyframes tranter-page-settle {
      from {
        scale: var(--page-media-scale);
      }
    }
    @keyframes tranter-page-fade {
      to {
        opacity: 0;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
